<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 15th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1400s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/15th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1450 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10232 5385" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1450 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="174"/><text x="5709" y="1043" font-size="209">1</text></g><g><circle cx="7643" cy="1242" r="174"/><text x="7643" y="1315" font-size="209">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5054" cy="728" r="174"/><text x="5054" y="801" font-size="209">3</text></g><g><circle cx="7752" cy="1900" r="174"/><text x="7752" y="1973" font-size="209">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7088" cy="1864" r="174"/><text x="7088" y="1937" font-size="209">5</text></g><g><circle cx="6029" cy="1964" r="174"/><text x="6029" y="2037" font-size="209">6</text></g><g><circle cx="7018" cy="1385" r="174"/><text x="7018" y="1458" font-size="209">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6582" cy="1190" r="174"/><text x="6582" y="1263" font-size="209">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1450 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Timurid Empire &middot; Ottoman Empire &middot; Ayutthaya Kingdom &middot; Ethiopian Empire &middot; Kingdom of France &middot; Vijayanagara Empire &middot; Ming Empire &middot; Delhi Sultanate</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Tordesillas</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Fall of Constantinople</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Great Stand on the Ugra River</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Agincourt</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Compromise of Caspe</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Morat</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Ivan III</li><li>Mehmed II</li><li>Christopher Columbus</li><li>Prince Henry the Navigator</li><li>Ferdinand II of Aragon</li><li>Philip the Good</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1440–1505</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1451–1506</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1432–1481</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1452–1516</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1396–1467</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1394–1460</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Sapa Inca</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Sugar plantation</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1400s, 236 recorded states were founded and 214 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Ottoman Empire, the Republic of Venice and the Ming Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 15th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/15th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 15th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Ottoman Empire <span>1299 CE – 1922 CE</span></li><li>Ming Empire <span>1368 CE – 1644 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of France <span>987 CE – 1792 CE</span></li><li>Ayutthaya Kingdom <span>1351 CE – 1767 CE</span></li><li>Vijayanagara Empire <span>1336 CE – 1646 CE</span></li><li>Ethiopian Empire <span>1270 CE – 1974 CE</span></li><li>Delhi Sultanate <span>1206 CE – 1526 CE</span></li><li>Timurid Empire <span>1363 CE – 1507 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Compromise of Caspe <span>1412</span></li><li>Battle of Agincourt <span>1415</span></li><li>Fall of Constantinople <span>1453</span></li><li>Battle of Morat <span>1476</span></li><li>Great Stand on the Ugra River <span>1480</span></li><li>Treaty of Tordesillas <span>1494</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Ivan III <span>1: 1440–1505</span></li><li>Mehmed II <span>3: 1432–1481</span></li><li>Christopher Columbus <span>2: 1451–1506</span></li><li>Prince Henry the Navigator <span>6: 1394–1460</span></li><li>Ferdinand II of Aragon <span>4: 1452–1516</span></li><li>Philip the Good <span>5: 1396–1467</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Sapa Inca</dt><dd>Sapa Inca, the 'unique Inca', was the title of the ruler of the Inca state.</dd><dt>Sugar plantation</dt><dd>A sugar plantation is a large agricultural estate growing sugarcane for sugar production, typically using intensive labour.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
